{
  "_about": "The rules of the learning game. Everything is derived from the progress a reader already has: modules marked done, and the day each mark was made (practice work is saved the same way, under the progress keys in site.config.json, so it syncs with the account like a module does). XP is paid for a module, a capstone (on top of its module), a whole track, a whole learning path, a coding problem, a daily drill, a quiz passed, a mock interview finished and a study plan finished. Levels are the XP needed to reach them. A badge is earned when its stat reaches atLeast; the stats are modules, capstones, tracks, paths, problems, drills, quizzes, mocks, plans and streak (days in a row). A quiz is passed (and paid for) from `quiz.passPercent` right. `levelCheck` the five-minute test that recommends where to start (the questions by area, drawn from the quizzes by topic, and the recommended path and plan for each area), `mock` the mock interviews (a track is quiz topics and coding topics, how many of each, how long it takes). The progress keys (site.config.json -> progressKeys) are stored in readers' progress and never change. This file is read only by the learning game (webapp/src/config/game.js), which is why it is not part of site.config.json: that file is in every visitor's first download.",
